WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.640
Robert Baratheon: For our rebellion to succeed,
King's Landing had to be taken, forcefully.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:13.850
No one was foolish enough to believe that
Aerys was gonna hand his crown over peacefully.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:18.140
The Mad King's reign needed to end.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:24.310
What Tywin Lannister's forces did was unfortunate,
but it was necessary to secure the Iron Throne,

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:28.410
and bring peace and justice to the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:34.190
My glorious victory at the Trident left me
wounded, but I sent my personal maester to

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:39.550
attend to Ser Barristan Selmy instead; his
wounds were more severe.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.180
Even though Ser Barristan was a member of
Aerys's Kingsguard and fought on the opposing

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:49.140
side, that man's bravery and loyalty were
something to behold.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:54.170
But this meant my wounds would take longer
to heal and I couldn't ride to King's Landing

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.559
myself.

00:00:55.559 --> 00:01:02.200
I sent the one man I trusted over anyone else
in this world, Ned Stark, in my place.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.930
Had I been able to ride, perhaps I could have
reached King's Landing sooner and prevented

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:11.340
some of the violence that occurred when the
Lannisters entered the city.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:15.920
Still, what Lord Tywin did was for the greater
good.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.500
Even what happened to Princess Elia and her
children.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:27.130
Babies or no, theirs was the same cursed blood
that flowed within the Mad King's veins.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:32.370
They were dragonspawn and couldn't be allowed
to survive.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.409
What would they grow to be?

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:36.040
Loyal subjects?

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.110
Ned, with his damn northern honor.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:47.229
He and I had our first major fight over the
deaths of the Targaryen children.

00:01:47.229 --> 00:01:49.610
Ned called it murder.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:50.780
Murder!?

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:54.600
It was war!...

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.640
It was war...

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:02.180
Lord Stark demanded that the Lannisters be
held responsible for their crimes.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:07.010
Was it a crime to put an end to a family of
lunatics born of incest?

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:09.880
I wouldn't - and still won't - blame Tywin.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:16.480
Instead, I sent Ned Stark south to finish
off the remaining Targaryen loyalists.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.040
It was only Lyanna Stark's death that reconciled
us.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.879
Ned had lost his sister.

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:27.370
I had lost my betrothed and beloved.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:31.989
We shared that sad bond together, Ned and
I.

00:02:31.989 --> 00:02:34.920
Through it, our friendship was made strong
again.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.590
Viserys Targaryen: The Battle of the Trident
may have been an important victory for the

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:45.760
Usurper, but it was the treachery and barbarism
of Tywin Lannister that sealed the fate of

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.450
the Targaryen dynasty.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:54.090
My father, King Aerys, had ever been a friend
to the Lions of the Rock.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:03:02.180
Aerys graciously brought Tywin to court, making
him the youngest Hand of the King in history.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.440
He gave him power.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.959
He gave him respect.

00:03:05.959 --> 00:03:11.190
He made it possible for Tywin to restore House
Lannister to glory.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:16.629
Aerys and Tywin governed side by side for
twenty prosperous years.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:22.349
Still, when the Usurper called his banners
in rebellion, Tywin Lannister ignored his

00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:28.190
king's pleas for help, and stayed holed up
in his stronghold of Casterly Rock.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:32.659
In time, my brother Prince Rhaegar was dead.

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:34.640
The realm was in turmoil.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:40.480
And the Usurper's forces were said to be riding
for King's Landing.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:46.220
What a glorious sight it must have been when
a force of ten thousand Lannister men showed

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:52.739
up at the gate of the capital with Lord Tywin
at their head, pledging support to his beleaguered

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:54.200
king.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.849
Aerys opened the gates for his old friend.

00:03:57.849 --> 00:04:04.530
Instead, Lannister and his men proceeded to
plunder and destroy the city that he had called

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:07.769
home for decades.

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:14.489
As the capital was ravaged and its people
terrorized, Jaime Lannister, son of Lord Tywin,

00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:17.660
proved every bit as treacherous.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:22.540
He killed my father, the king, at the foot
of the Iron Throne.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:27.220
The Lannisters entered the Red Keep and Tywin
ordered the deaths of the rest of the royal

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.190
family.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:35.830
It is said Princess Rhaenys was found cowering
under her father's bed and put to the sword.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.470
She was only a child.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:44.530
As for Rhaegar's widow, Elia, she was forced
to watch as Lannister thugs dashed her baby

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:50.410
son's head against a wall, before being murdered
herself.

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:55.000
As I was the heir to my father's throne, I
had been spirited away to Dragonstone with

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.680
my mother, Queen Rhaella, who was with child.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:03.840
As a raging summer storm battered the island
fortress and destroyed the Targaryen fleet

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:09.210
as it lay at anchor, my sister Daenerys was
born.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:12.550
My mother, the queen, died giving birth.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:17.680
Maester Luwin: Robert Baratheon's victory
at the Trident was a turning point in the

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.770
war for the Iron Throne.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:25.030
While it was clear the gods were smiling on
the rebel forces, Aerys Targaryen still held

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:27.270
the Red Keep at King's Landing.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:33.430
As Robert was wounded and unable to ride,
it was up to Eddard Stark to make for the

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:38.700
capital and force the Mad King to give up
the throne.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:45.390
Lord Stark reached the city gates to find
that Tywin Lannister, Lord of Casterly Rock,

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.770
had already sacked the city in Robert's name.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:53.430
House Lannister had remained neutral up to
this point, ignoring requests for help from

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:55.889
both the crown and the rebels.

00:05:55.889 --> 00:06:03.080
Now that Robert's eventual victory was assured,
it seemed Lord Tywin had finally chosen a

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.199
side.

00:06:04.199 --> 00:06:09.630
Lord Eddard was horrified by what he saw when
he entered the city - homes looted and burned,

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:12.039
scores of innocent citizens killed.

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:16.960
Disgusted, he led his force up Visenya's Hill
to the Red Keep.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:23.289
Upon entering the throne room, he found King
Aerys lying in a pool of blood... dead, by

00:06:23.289 --> 00:06:32.610
the hand of his own sworn Kingsguard, Jaime
Lannister - who sat brazenly upon the throne.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:37.630
Demanding to know the whereabouts of Queen
Rhaella, Lord Eddard was informed the queen

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:43.710
and her son Viserys had been spirited away
to Dragonstone before the Lannisters arrived.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:47.210
But other members of the royal family were
not as fortunate.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:53.759
Elia Martell of Dorne, who was the wife of
Prince Rhaegar, had been murdered by Ser Gregor

00:06:53.759 --> 00:06:56.840
Clegane on Lord Tywin's orders.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:01.160
Ser Gregor and his men had also butchered
Rhaegar's young children.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:06.569
When Robert was well enough to reach the capital,
Lord Eddard demanded the Lannisters answer

00:07:06.569 --> 00:07:08.980
for their heinous crimes.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:15.169
Robert refused, and sent himself to relieve
the Baratheon stronghold of Storm's End, which

00:07:15.169 --> 00:07:19.300
was still under siege by forces loyal to the
crown.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:24.220
Whatever words passed between the two old
friends are known only to them, but Lord Eddard

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:27.710
is said to have left King's Landing in anger.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:33.580
Later, when Robert was crowned, he appointed
Jon Arryn as Hand of the King.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:38.700
Lord Arryn's first order of business was to
broker a truce with the Martells of Dorne,

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:43.600
who were outraged by the brutal murder of
Princess Elia and her children.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:49.000
Following the death of Lyanna Stark, who had
been betrothed to Robert, Houses Baratheon

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:54.340
and Lannister were joined in marriage when
the new king took Tywin Lannister's eldest

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:57.410
daughter, Cersei, as his queen.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:08:04.319
As for Eddard Stark, he returned to his stronghold
of Winterfell, forever haunted by his sister's

00:08:04.319 --> 00:08:08.930
death, and the shameful way that Robert had
secured his throne.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:15.389
Tywin Lannister: Rhaegar Targaryen lay dead
on the banks of the Trident, his royal army

00:08:15.389 --> 00:08:18.539
shattered and in retreat.

00:08:18.539 --> 00:08:21.879
The days of the dragon kings were clearly
numbered.

00:08:21.879 --> 00:08:27.680
Until that moment it would have been foolish
to commit Casterly Rock to either the crown

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:30.990
or the rebellion.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:37.039
What would our family have to gain in supporting
a raving madman or in entering a crusade to

00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:40.750
put Robert Baratheon on the Iron Throne?

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.870
But chaos benefits no one.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:49.430
It was time for House Lannister to do what
it could to ensure a return of peace and prosperity

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:51.200
to the land.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:57.570
I, Tywin Lannister, brought ten thousand Lannister
troops to the gates of King's Landing, in

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:02.420
order to bring the bloodshed to a quick and
decisive conclusion.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:07.940
King Aerys had been sending ravens for months
begging for my support to end the uprising.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:12.630
In a way, his pleas had been answered.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:19.560
As I had suspected, Aerys opened the city
gates and welcomed my men.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:25.590
Our plan was clear: crush Aerys's remaining
bannermen and remove the remnants of the royal

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:30.320
family as quickly and efficiently as possible.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:37.510
Any alternative meant years of further war
and a fragmented Seven Kingdoms.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:43.800
Our means were bloody, but the results speak
for themselves.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:50.170
As for Aerys, it is true he met his fate at
the hands of my son.

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:55.500
Aerys had kept Jaime close during the rebellion,
thinking himself clever in keeping my son

00:09:55.500 --> 00:10:01.190
as a hostage - should I decide to pledge support
to the rebel cause.

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:08.940
This proved to be his greatest mistake, for
when the time came Jaime did his duty as a

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:13.180
Lannister... and drove his sword into the
Mad King's back.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:18.540
With that, Robert Baratheon's crown was secured.

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:24.990
The new king recognized our role in his ascension
to the throne, just as he recognized how useful

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:32.209
the might and riches of Casterly Rock would
be... if he wanted to keep it.

00:10:32.209 --> 00:10:36.480
To that end, I offered my daughter Cersei
as his queen.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:42.950
Had Aerys not spurned this same offer years
earlier, perhaps things would have worked

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:44.920
out differently.

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:50.220
With Robert and Cersei crowned as King and
Queen of the Seven Kingdoms, it was a new

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.779
day.

00:10:51.779 --> 00:10:59.540
The dragon was vanquished, and the Seven Kingdoms
would thereafter belong to the stag... and

00:10:59.540 --> 00:10:59.920
the lion.

